# Run SYNTRA (Flutter + Cloud Run)

Default run is **Chrome + Cloud Run + Firebase Auth**. Do not use local ADK unless the user explicitly asks for local-only.

```bash
cd frontends/syntra_app
flutter run -d chrome --dart-define-from-file=firebase.defines.json
```

Do **not** set `ADK_BASE_URL`. `AdkConfig` defaults to Cloud Run:
`https://syntra-orchestrator-459448503831.us-central1.run.app`

## Do not

- `./scripts/dev.sh` (starts local ADK and `--dart-define=ADK_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000`)
- `flutter run --dart-define=ADK_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000`
- `flutter run` without `--dart-define-from-file=firebase.defines.json` (Sign in shows "Add firebase.defines.json")
- Treat **Skip for now** / guest as the default when the user wants to sign in

## Firebase defines

Use local `frontends/syntra_app/firebase.defines.json` (gitignored). Do not commit it. Do not invent dummy API keys.

If the file is missing: look at `frontends/syntra_app/firebase.defines.example.json` and `frontends/syntra_app/README.md`; fill real values from the Firebase console or FlutterFire output on this machine. Do not fabricate credentials.

Agent deploys stay in `.cursor/rules/cloud-run-deploy.mdc` (`./scripts/deploy_cloud_run.sh`).
